[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Englund Gambit"]
[Variation "4.Bf4 Qb4+ 5.Nc3"]
[ECO "A40"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap"]
[Themes "queen-pressure,development-lead"]

1. d4 e5 { The Englund Gambit: Black offers a pawn at once to pull White's centre apart and get tricky play. } 2. dxe5 2... Nc6 { Attacks the e5 pawn, so Black wins it back unless White finds a way to defend it. }
3. Nf3 3... Qe7 { Attacks e5 a second time and prepares ...Qb4+, which will hit the b2 pawn and any loose piece. [%cal Ge7e5,Ge7b4] }
4. Bf4 4... Qb4+ { Check, and the queen also attacks the bishop on f4, so White cannot do everything at once. [%cal Gb4e1,Gb4f4] }
5. Nc3?! { A developing block, but it leaves the bishop to be taken. The engine prefers 5.Bd2, which leads to the trap in the refutations folder. } 5... Qxf4 { Takes the bishop. White's next move is a knight jump, so Black has to be accurate. }
6. Nd5 6... Qe4 { Attacks the knight on d5 and keeps the queen in the centre. [%cal Ge4d5] } 7. Nxc7+ 7... Kd8 8. Nxa8 8... Nxe5 { Takes the pawn back and attacks the knight on f3. Black has given up a rook but White's knight is nearly trapped. }
9. Qd2 9... b6 { Traps the knight on a8: ...Bb7 next would win it. [%cal Gb6a8] } 10. O-O-O 10... Nxf3 11. exf3 11... Qxa8 12. Bc4 *
